RELION 5 (7f45a711): the two weighted-sum CPU kernels (wavg_ref3D, backprojectRef3D) skip what adds nothing. Only
samples at or above significant_weight enter the sums, yet both kernels project or walk every fine orientation and
build sin/cos tables for every translation. An orientation without such a sample is skipped whole and a translation
without one gets no table. Every sum is the same to the bit (perf/rlx/wsum/same_sums.py on two records).

